# Look and feel

One system. Pages do not pick their own colors, type, or spacing.

## Tokens

Define brand, type, space, and radius once in `src/styles/main.css` using Tailwind 4 `@theme`. Components use those tokens (`bg-surface`, `text-ink`, `font-display`), never raw hex after tokens exist.

Direction: quiet industrial B2B with a dynamic opening. Light surfaces, dark ink, one accent. Strong headings, short body. Full-bleed photo heroes with type on a dark scrim. No playful display fonts, neon gradients, glassmorphism, or app-chrome (DaisyUI).

## Chrome

- Every page: `SiteHeader` + `SiteFooter` via `PageShell`.
- Header overlays photo heroes (white logo), then turns solid on scroll. One max-width container (`AppContainer`).
- Section vertical rhythm from `AppSection` (`py-12 md:py-16`, compact `py-8 md:py-12`). Do not put one-off `py-*` on a page band. Adjacent same-tone bands collapse the second top pad so padding does not double.
- Type scale shared: eyebrow, h1, h2, body, caption. Headings through `AppHeading` (`tone="inverse"` on photo and ink).
- Buttons only through `AppButton`: `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `outline-light` (on photo heroes). One size scale.
- Links that are buttons use `AppButton`; text links use `AppLink` (internal or external with `noopener`).

## Motion and media

- Allowed: desktop parallax on photo heroes, one-shot section arrival, interactive process loop, hover/tap detail on feature cards, media sliders without autoplay.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`: turn parallax and fades off; keep loop and slider usable.
- One full-bleed hero per page (`HeroSection`). Do not invent a second hero component.
- Images: real operations photography and perspective-warped product screens, explicit width/height, lazy below the fold, WebP. No unlabeled stock.

## Responsive

Mobile-first Tailwind. Header, hero, and footer must work at a phone width and a desktop width. Verify both when layout changes.

## Accessibility

Semantic landmarks (`header`, `main`, `footer`, `nav`). Visible focus rings (do not `outline-none` without a replacement). Contrast that meets WCAG AA. Do not ship `v-html` of untrusted strings.
